---
const levels = [
  { n: 1, name: "Text", body: "Which lines changed. This is git diff." },
  { n: 2, name: "Structure", body: "Which functions, classes and statements changed, ignoring formatting and moved code." },
  { n: 3, name: "Relationships", body: "Which connections changed: new calls, new data flows, new dependencies, changed contracts." },
  { n: 4, name: "Behavior", body: "Which inputs now produce different outputs, as shown by tests and traces." },
];
---

<section class="section wrap levels" id="how" aria-labelledby="levels-title">
  <h2 class="section-title" id="levels-title">Review what changed in meaning, not in text.</h2>
  <p class="prose lead">
    A line diff tells you which characters changed. A reviewer needs to know what the system now does
    differently, and line count barely tracks risk.
  </p>

  <div class="pair">
    <figure class="mini">
      <figcaption class="subhead">Rename a function used in 40 files</figcaption>
      <div class="mini-diff">
        <span class="m-del">- const total = formatOrderTotal(order);</span>
        <span class="m-add">+ const total = formatTotal(order);</span>
        <span class="m-del">- export function formatOrderTotal(o: Order)</span>
        <span class="m-add">+ export function formatTotal(o: Order)</span>
        <span class="m-more">  …and 38 more files</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mini-verdict"><strong>412 lines changed.</strong> Behavior changed: none.</p>
    </figure>

    <figure class="mini">
      <figcaption class="subhead">Change one operator in a discount check</figcaption>
      <div class="mini-diff">
        <span class="m-del">- if (subtotal &gt; threshold) &#123;</span>
        <span class="m-add">+ if (subtotal &gt;= threshold) &#123;</span>
        <span class="m-ctx">    return applyDiscount(order);</span>
        <span class="m-ctx">  &#125;</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mini-verdict">
        <strong>1 character changed.</strong> Every order exactly at the threshold now gets a discount.
        In a permissions check, the same character could open a door.
      </p>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="stack">
    <p class="prose">
      There are four levels at which you can describe a change. Onus puts levels 3 and 4 in front of
      reviewers, with levels 1 and 2 one click away. It also checks the agent's stated intent against what
      the change actually does: if an agent says it only touched logging and the report shows a new write
      to the payments table, that mismatch goes to the top.
    </p>
    <ol class="level-list">
      {
        levels.map((l) => (
          <li class={`level ${l.n >= 3 ? "is-surface" : ""}`}>
            <span class="level-n" aria-hidden="true">{l.n}</span>
            <div>
              <p class="level-name">
                {l.name}
                {l.n >= 3 ? <span class="tag">Review surface</span> : <span class="tag tag-quiet">One click away</span>}
              </p>
              <p class="level-body">{l.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lead {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .pair {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 22rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .mini {
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-panel);
    padding: clamp(1rem, 0.7rem + 1.2vw, 1.6rem);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .mini-diff {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    overflow-x: auto;
    background: var(--paper-2);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
  }

  .mini-diff span {
    display: block;
    white-space: pre;
    padding-inline: 0.85rem;
  }

  .m-add {
    background: var(--add-bg);
  }

  .m-del {
    background: var(--del-bg);
  }

  .m-more,
  .m-ctx {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .mini-verdict {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-top: auto;
  }

  .stack {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 3vw, 4.5rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem 3.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .stack {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .level-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .level {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem 0.9rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-strip);
    border: 1px dashed var(--rule);
  }

  .level.is-surface {
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-paper);
    border-left: 8px solid var(--cobalt);
  }

  .level-n {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-stretch: 120%;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .is-surface .level-n {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .level-name {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .level-body {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
  }

  .tag {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--cobalt);
  }

  .tag-quiet {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
</style>
